r for 21 so my total October 2019  including my insurance premium for this  appendectomy  two thousand  876 dollars just a few interesting items  from my itemized bill there's so much  more to it but just a few things I found  notable when I arrived they said hey  listen we should just we don't know  what's going on yet but anytime people  come in we try to keep them hydrated so  we're gonna give you an IV I said sure  that was 188 dollars I I'm glad they did  it I mean it does seem like a good  practice but that nearly $200 for the  saline bag  a seed the CT scan of course they needed  to do a CT scan to determine if I have  appendicitis that was more than $2,000  billed to insurance the IV tylenol I was  given before the procedure was a hundred  and fifty three dollars and you know  they didn't leave me in the hallway they  brought me to a recovery room after the  procedure that was six hundred and  seventy eight dollars now what's  interesting about that is they said that  because they would probably only keep me  a few hours after the procedure they  didn't need to bring me upstairs to a  room now if I was brought upstairs to a  room we would be talking about thousands  more dollars because that would be  considered being admitted to the  hospital they didn't do that instead  they put me in the recovery room for  ninety minutes  that was 678 much cheaper than bringing  me up to a room so once again what's the  big picture here the nurses were great  top-notch surgeon anesthesiologist was  great everyone's bedside manner was  great they treated my girlfriend really  well even after as I was already on  valium and being wheeled in I yelled out  I hope I don't die which was not exactly  in confidence inspiring to her at the  time they treated her well they treated  me well but this is an insane system now  I want to be really clear owing $2,800  it's not going to bankrupt me right I I  always assumed that at any time because  of the insurance I have with the $2,000